    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The narrative centers on strengthening commercial traction, with the company’s non-invasive neuromodulation therapies gaining momentum in the U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs channel—its largest growth driver—as well as through emerging consumer wellness offerings. Reports indicate expanding adoption across VA facilities and a growing patient base, while newer products are carving out a meaningful presence alongside the legacy prescription device. Market commentary points to an improving demand environment, though the company remains in an investment phase, still posting net losses despite rapid top-line expansion.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is emphasizing evidence of emerging operating leverage, driven by a high-margin product mix and disciplined cost management that has narrowed adjusted losses. The team reaffirmed its full-year growth outlook, signaling confidence in the current trajectory. Strategic moves to broaden the product portfolio and deepen institutional penetration are being highlighted as key to building a sustainable business, though the path to profitability remains a central watchpoint. Overall, the tone suggests management is executing on its plan and maintaining credibility with the market during a period of record performance.",
